body:
## Construct

Absence: `null`, `undefined`, `??`, `?.` and JSDoc unions such as `{string|null}`. The portable core refuses all of them (`null: outside the portable core`). Idiomatic JavaScript returns `null` from every lookup and parser, so this blocks most functions that can fail.

## Count in formal-ai

- `null`: **162**
- `nullish coalescing`: **25**
- `optional chaining`: **19**
- `undefined`: **12**

Together that is **218** carried items. Part of the 198 `JSDoc type {…}` refusals are `{T|null}` too. The wider measurement counts 543, 65, 25 and 50.

## Minimal input

```js
/**
 * @param {string} text
 * @returns {string|null}
 */
export function nonEmpty(text) {
  if (text === '') return null;
  return text;
}

/** @param {string} text @returns {string} */
export function orDefault(text) {
  return nonEmpty(text) ?? 'default';
}

/** @param {string} text @returns {boolean} */
export function isEmpty(text) {
  return nonEmpty(text) === null;
}
```

## Expected Rust

```rust
pub fn nonEmpty(text: String) -> Option<String> {
    if text == "" {
        None
    } else {
        Some(text)
    }
}

pub fn orDefault(text: String) -> String {
    nonEmpty(text).unwrap_or_else(|| String::from("default"))
}

pub fn isEmpty(text: String) -> bool {
    nonEmpty(text).is_none()
}
```

## Suggested direction

- `T|null`, `T|undefined` and `?T` map to `Option<T>`.
- `=== null` and `!== null` map to `is_none` and `is_some`.
- `?? b` maps to `unwrap_or` or `unwrap_or_else`.
- `x?.f` maps to `.as_ref().map(|x| x.f)`.
- An unannotated `null` gets its type from flow inference.

The other targets already have option types (`Option` in Lean, `option` in Rocq), so the encoding stays four-language.

---

**Where this comes from.** [formal-ai](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai) translates its JavaScript modules to Rust with `selfTranslate(source, 'JavaScript', 'Rust')` from meta-language `main` at `679a3b3c` (PR #196), through [`scripts/translate-js-rust.mjs`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/a75bf377287664599d506921a30bd3bc37410022/scripts/translate-js-rust.mjs). In scope are 128 modules (`js/agentic/crate/*.mjs` and the meta reasoner): 249 of 2,369 top-level items translate and 2,120 are carried. The census counts the construct `translateProgram` names first for each carried item: [`data/meta/js-rust-translation.lino`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/a75bf377287664599d506921a30bd3bc37410022/data/meta/js-rust-translation.lino). The per-item projections are in [`rust/tests/fixtures/js-rust-translation/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/a75bf377287664599d506921a30bd3bc37410022/rust/tests/fixtures/js-rust-translation). A wider measurement adds the agentic planner, the server and the browser worker, 232 more modules: 819 of 6,556 items translate there.

The repro above was checked with `selfTranslate` at `679a3b3c`. The umbrella for this work is #199, section 1. This issue is the one construct, with a minimal case to test against.
